LingTu's 2026 adaptation includes immutable OctoMap columns, separate inferred
support and occupied-height acceleration blocks. On 2026-11-08 the shared
implementation moved from the global planner to Maps. Per-height morphological
closing was replaced by bounded-hole selection, local observed-boundary plane
fitting and known-free exclusion. No CuPy/OpenCV/Rust implementation was copied.

The bounded internal-hole selection was informed by the MIT-licensed
elevation_mapping_cupy ROS2 inpainting implementation at
d9e1c9fe42ea3d463519333a443da99f680adde8. LingTu's implementation keeps distinct
3D heights and evaluates original OctoMap evidence instead of image inpainting.

